the added cost for groceries and gas  forcing a lot of families to have to  make some pretty difficult decisions and  some are realizing they just simply  cannot afford to keep up with the cost  associated with caring for their pet  which leads to abandonment and  surrendering in fact a local rescue  group believes that's why two pit bulls  were left tied to trees over the weekend  victoria saha joining us now in studio  with more on this growing issue victoria  denise you just can't help but wonder  how someone could abandon their pets  like that but it's a sad reality that's  becoming all too common overwhelming our  shelters so far this month the animal  foundation has taken in at least 90  animals every day  abandonment is really never ever a  legitimate excuse or option kelly winder  runs rescue missions across the valley  to get pets off our streets over the  weekend he responded when these two pit  bulls were found tied up to trees  besides shock it's anger there was no  doubt in winder's mind the pit bulls  were abandoned it's an option for the  lazy uneducated  and  the people that are ignorant of the  resources out there the dogs were taken  to the animal foundation where over 1300  animals were brought in just in the  first two weeks of june this includes  strays confiscations and surrenders the  last time they had that many was in 2019  but in 2020 the number was drastically  low as a lot of people got a pet during  the pandemic we knew  a storm was coming and it's not going to  be an easy fix four-year-old mona lisa  was amongst their surrenders this month  we met her just as she got adopted on  monday inflation is hurting everybody  let's be honest  and it doesn't matter whether you have a  lot of money or a little bit of money  owner mikhail lerma wanted to take a  chance on mona lisa despite the rising  cost of necessities just because the  world's gonna have issues doesn't mean i  can't help a dog out no one knows why  mona lisa was surrendered but as she  drives away to her forever home there  are hundreds of animals waiting for the  same  outcome  the animal foundation says owners often  don't disclose why they're surrendering  a pet but if it is for financial issues  they have programs that will help feed  and take care of your pets needs and you  do not need to meet a certain income  bracket we do have that information up  on our website at eight news now dot com  as for those two pit bulls that were  abandoned winder says one of them was  microchipped but the owner has not come  forward brian victoria thank you for  that
 

